Description: Perl script argument and option processing
 OptArgs2 processes command line arguments, options, and subcommands
 for Perl scripts. Its features are a superset of the core Getopt::Long
 module:
 .
    * Clear declarative API
    * Decoded argument processing (not just --options!)
    * Option aliases, hidden options
    * Default coderefs, Triggers
    * Auto-generated usage messages
 .
 The distribution also includes support for CLI status lines and for
 sending output to a system pager.
